 "title": "Menominee County | Departments » Register of Deeds",
 "text": "Menominee County | Departments » Register of Deeds\nGovernment\nAgendas & Minutes\nBoards & Committees\nEmployment\nForms & Documents\nMunicipalities\nServices\nDepartments\n9-1-1 (Central Dispatch)\nAdministration\nBuilding Codes\nClerk\nCounty Board of Commissioners\nCounty Fair\nCourts\nEmergency Management\nEqualization\nFriend of the Court\nLand Information Services (GIS)\nMenominee County Library\nMenominee Regional Airport\nParks & Recreation\nProsecuting Attorney\nRegister of Deeds\nRoad Commission\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nVeteran Services\nCommunity\nArea Information\nCUPPAD\nM & M Regional Guide\nMenominee Conservation District\nMenominee County 4-H\nMichigan Department of Health & Human Services\nMichigan State University - Extension\nNorthpointe Behavioral Health\nPublic Health - Delta & Menominee Counties\nUPCAP - Upper Peninsula Commission for Area Progress\nMore\nCalendar\nContact Us\nEmail Alerts\nFAQ\nLinks\nNews\nStaff Directory\n-->\nREGISTER OF DEEDS |\n|\n• General Information |\n|\n- |\n|\nStaff |\n|\n- |\n|\nContact Us |\n|\n• Free Fraud Alert Services |\n|\n• Passport |\n|\n• Recording Requirements and Fees |\n|\n• Transfer Tax |\n|\n• Title/Abstract Companies |\n|\n-->\n- Select Section --> REGISTER OF DEEDS General Information Staff Contact Us Free Fraud Alert Services Passport Recording Requirements and Fees Transfer Tax Title/Abstract Companies DEPARTMENTS HOME\nRegister of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds office is where all deeds and mortgages of properties within Menominee County are filed. The Tract Index which is kept in this office's vault is a history of each parcel of land. It starts with the first acquisition of land deeded from the United States government to the first settler or buyer. It then lists all deed/mortgage transactions recorded on the parcel of land from then to the present day.\nThere is internet access available through the Land Records link. Viewing or printing these records can be done by subscribing for the service.\nTax liens, Sheriff's deeds and U.C.C.'s are also filed in this office. A record of all the County Board meetings - the Book of Minutes - is kept on record in the Register's vault. This is a log of all the activities, motions and resolutions to name a few, from the earliest days of Menominee County as a new government entity.\nContact: |\nMarc Kleiman - County Register of Deeds\nPhone: (906) 863-2822\nClick here to email |\nMailing Address: |\n839 10th Avenue\nMenominee, MI 49858\nMap |\nPhysical Address: |\n839 10th Avenue - 1st floor\nMenominee, MI 49858\nMap |\nHours: |\n8:00 am - 4:30 pm\nMonday through Friday\n(open during lunch hour)\nClosed on Holidays |\nCopyright © 2026 Menominee County\nGovernment - Menominee Michigan\nMenominee County Courthouse\n839 10th Avenue\nMenominee, MI 49858\n(906) 863-7779\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Notice\nAcceptable Use Policy\nLinking Policy\nDesigned & Powered By:",
